\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Graphical overview of MD-CBAD-DQN\xspace  . Simulator-exact analytical previews expose the immediate cost and six post-action resources for all three scheduling actions. Centering the resulting Bellman targets isolates action-relative supervision. The factual standard-DQN target and loss term are retained, and the auxiliary loss contributes an additional gradient during training. The illustration is conceptual and encodes no quantitative results.\relax }}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:graphical}{{1}{2}{Graphical overview of \method . Simulator-exact analytical previews expose the immediate cost and six post-action resources for all three scheduling actions. Centering the resulting Bellman targets isolates action-relative supervision. The factual standard-DQN target and loss term are retained, and the auxiliary loss contributes an additional gradient during training. The illustration is conceptual and encodes no quantitative results.\relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
