\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Training-only CBAD mechanism. The upper path retains the factual standard-DQN target and Huber loss. The lower path previews all three actions, constructs three Bellman targets, centers them within state, and distills their relative advantages. Both losses update the online Q-network; the target network is synchronized only at the shared fixed interval. Preview outputs are unavailable during evaluation and deployment.\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{4}{10}{Training-only CBAD mechanism. The upper path retains the factual standard-DQN target and Huber loss. The lower path previews all three actions, constructs three Bellman targets, centers them within state, and distills their relative advantages. Both losses update the online Q-network; the target network is synchronized only at the shared fixed interval. Preview outputs are unavailable during evaluation and deployment.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
